        'Credibility also requires that those who audit others submit first to audit themselves. As the closing essay of our Inaugural Edition, we state without ambiguity that **Kashmir EcoWatch and Himalayan Dispatch enjoy zero exemption from universal standards**. An independent observatory can fail through subtle biases of its own: over-covering photogenic alpine valleys while neglecting Jammu’s *kandi* belt or industrial estates; confusing modelled remote-sensing estimates with field-verified ground truth; or allowing civic sympathy to soften scrutiny of local encroachments. Accordingly, we bind our masthead permanently to four self-governance rules: (1) commissioning investigations across every project sector without political, commercial, or sectarian fear or favour; (2) publishing explicit methodological uncertainty bounds and Stage 05 external peer-review statuses on every scientific synthesis; (3) guaranteeing full, unedited right of reply and transparent post-publication corrections to every agency, shrine board, enterprise, NGO, and community; and (4) refusing all political-party, corporate-concessionaire, or conditional donor funding.',
